Z||000000||Fiero*101||12-15-2001||10:58 AM||||But it has to do with technicals too.<BR>Im looking thru the calssifiedes today and i look at this add from a guy that lives about 45 min to an hour away from me, and he is selling a 1984 Fiero 4 tech 4 speed for $100.00 it doesnt give any info at all on the car except for it says low miles<P>Now i ask all you wonderful PFF people what could be wrong with this car if he only wants to sell it for a 100 dollars?<P>I want some opinons first before i give him a call.<P>Any ideas?<P>------------------<BR>Fiero*101<BR>Gold 86 SE 2M6<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mycar101.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||12-15-2001||11:17 AM||||Maybe he just assumes with as old as it is, It's not worth much. Any Fiero that runs is worth it. I would call and ask for more info.<BR>Ask things like how are the brakes, clutch, engine, etc. For $100 you probably are not worried about faded paint or the ripped seat.<BR>If it's drivable I say "go for it".<P>------------------<BR>             <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">           <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Happiness isn't around the corner...<BR>Happiness IS the corner.</I></B></FONT>||||reg||1
